    "member_id": "snowflake-session-query-acceleration-invalid-20261013"
  },
  "context": "Found 2026-10-13 in the local bundle tpch_sf1_snowflake_sql_20261012_172155_3067b960 (statement 4 of 7, status failed); the same failed statement appears in every 2026-10-12 Snowflake bundle.",
  "description": "## Problem\nFor OLAP, TPC-H and TPC-DS runs, `configure_for_benchmark` issues `ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_ACCELERATION_MAX_SCALE_FACTOR = 8` (`benchbox/platforms/snowflake.py:1046`, present since the initial release). That is a warehouse property, not a session parameter. Snowflake rejects it with `001006 (22023): SQL compilation error: invalid parameter 'QUERY_ACCELERATION_MAX_SCALE_FACTOR'`.\n\nEvery Snowflake bundle from 2026-10-12 records it as a failed session statement in `platform.tuning.applied.statements`. That adds noise to the applied-tuning ledger, and readers may mistake it for a tuning failure.\n\n## Change\n- Remove the statement from the session settings.\n- If query acceleration should be configured, do it only under `modify_warehouse_settings` as `ALTER WAREHOUSE ... SET QUERY_ACCELERATION_MAX_SCALE_FACTOR`, which is a warehouse change gated by that flag.\n- Update or add a unit test asserting the session statements.",
  "links": [
    "benchbox/platforms/snowflake.py"
  ],
